            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Immunoprecipitation Is a Rapid Affinity Purification Method 486  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Genetically Engineered Tags Provide an Easy Way to Purify Proteins 486  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Purified Cell-free Systems Are Required for the Precise Dissection of Molecular Functions 486  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Summary 487  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "ANALYZING PROTEINS 487  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Proteins Can Be Separated by SDS Polyacrylamide-Gel Electrophoresis 487  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Two-dimensional Gel Electrophoresis Provides Greater Protein Separation 489  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Specific Proteins Can Be Detected by Blotting with Antibodies 490  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Hydrodynamic Measurements Reveal the Size and Shape of a Protein Complex 490  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Mass Spectrometry Provides a Highly Sensitive Method for Identifying Unknown Proteins 491  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Sets of Interacting Proteins Can Be Identified by Biochemical Methods 493  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Optical Methods Can Monitor Protein Interactions 493  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Protein Structure Can Be Determined Using X-ray Diffraction 494  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "NMR Can Be Used to Determine Protein Structure in Solution 496  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Protein Sequence and Structure Provide Clues About Protein Function 497  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Summary 498  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "ANALYZING AND MANIPULATING DNA 498  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Restriction Nucleases Cut Large DNA Molecules into Specific Fragments 498  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Gel Electrophoresis Separates DNA Molecules of Different Sizes 499  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Purified DNA Molecules Can Be Specifically Labeled with Radioisotopes or Chemical Markers in Vitro 501  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Genes Can Be Cloned Using Bacteria 501  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "An Entire Genome Can Be Represented in a DNA Library 503  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Hybridization Provides a Powerful but Simple Way to Detect Specific Nucleotide Sequences 505  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Genes Can Be Cloned in Vitro Using PCR 506  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "PCR Is Also Used for Diagnostic and Forensic Applications 507  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "PCR and Synthetic DNA Are Ideal Sources of Specific Gene Sequences for Cloning 510  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "DNA Cloning Allows Any Protein to Be Produced in Large Amounts 511  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "DNA Can Be Sequenced Rapidly by Dideoxy Sequencing 512  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Next-Generation Sequencing Methods Have Revolutionized DNA and RNA Analysis 514  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "To Be Useful, Genome Sequences Must Be Annotated 516  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Summary 518  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "STUDYING GENE FUNCTION AND EXPRESSION 518  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Classical Genetic Screens Identify Random Mutants with Specific Abnormalities 519  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Mutations Can Cause Loss or Gain of Protein Function 522  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Complementation Tests Reveal Whether Two Mutations Are in the Same Gene or Different Genes 523  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Gene Products Can Be Ordered in Pathways by Epistasis Analysis 523  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Mutations Responsible for a Phenotype Can Be Identified Through DNA Analysis 524  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Rapid and Cheap DNA Sequencing Has Revolutionized Human Genetic Studies 524  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Linked Blocks of Polymorphisms Have Been Passed Down from Our Ancestors 525  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Sequence Variants Can Aid the Search for Mutations Associated with Disease 526  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Genomics Is Accelerating the Discovery of Rare Mutations That Predispose Us to Serious Disease 527  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The Cellular Functions of a Known Gene Can Be Studied with Genome Engineering 527  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Animals and Plants Can Be Genetically Altered 528  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The Bacterial CRISPR System Has Been Adapted to Edit Genomes in a Wide Variety of Species 530  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Large Collections of Engineered Mutations Provide a Tool for Examining the Function of Every Gene in an Organism 531  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "RNA Interference Is a Simple and Rapid Way to Test Gene Function 533  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Reporter Genes Reveal When and Where a Gene Is Expressed 534  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "In Situ Hybridization Can Reveal the Location of mRNAs and Noncoding RNAs 535"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "index",
