          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "LOOKING AT CELLS AND MOLECULES IN THE LIGHT MICROSCOPE 563  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The Conventional Light Microscope Can Resolve Details "
                },
                {
                  "type": "equation_inline",
                  "content": "0.2\\mu \\mathrm{m}"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": " Apart 564  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Photon Noise Creates Additional Limits to Resolution When Light Levels Are Low 567  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Living Cells Are Seen Clearly in a Phase-Contrast or a Differential-Interference-Contrast Microscope 567  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Images Can Be Enhanced and Analyzed by Digital Techniques 568  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Intact Tissues Are Usually Fixed and Sectioned Before Microscopy 569  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Specific Molecules Can Be Located in Cells by Fluorescence Microscopy 570  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Antibodies Can Be Used to Detect Specific Proteins 572  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Individual Proteins Can Be Fluorescently Tagged in Living Cells and Organisms 573  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Protein Dynamics Can Be Followed in Living Cells 575  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fluorescent Biosensors Can Monitor Cell Signaling 576  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Imaging of Complex Three-dimensional Objects Is Possible with the Optical Microscope 577  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "The Confocal Microscope Produces Optical Sections by Excluding Out-of-Focus Light 578  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Superresolution Fluorescence Techniques Can Overcome Diffraction-limited Resolution 580  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Single-Molecule Localization Microscopy Also Delivers Superresolution 583  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Expanding the Specimen Can Offer Higher Resolution, but with a Conventional Microscope 585  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Large Multicellular Structures Can Be Imaged Over Time 586  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Single Molecules Can Be Visualized by Total Internal Reflection Fluorescence Microscopy 587  "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Summary 588"
                }
              ]
            }
